<title>LITHUANIA: YIELD UP AT 29-DAY T-BILL AUCTION.</title>
<headline>YIELD UP AT 29-DAY T-BILL AUCTION.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on short-term 29-day</p>
<p>government Treasury bills rose on Monday, hitting 7.38 percent</p>
<p>after 7.25 percent at the previous auction.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AV YIELD   LAST TIME   MIN/MAX   ISSUE   BID  SOLD</p>
<p> 29-day	7.38	 7.25	7.25/7.48   30    63.409 30</p>
<p>The settlement date for today's auction was July 31 and the</p>
<p>bills mature on August 29.</p>
<p>The next auction will be on July 29, when 60 million litas</p>
<p>of 364-day paper will be sold.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
